  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-133914\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><div id=\"graphic-q-133914-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-133914-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>We note the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a <em>negative</em> slope. So, we have a <em>negative</em> correlation.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, we have a <em>weak</em> correlation.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the variables have a <em>weak negative</em> linear correlation.</p>\n</div>",
